  colors: bg=BLACK(0), obstacle=ORANGE(7), marker=MAGENTA(6)
  markers:
    count: 1-3, placed on bottom row (row H-1), no obstacle at same cell
    columns must be distinct
  obstacles:
    scattered ORANGE pixels throughout grid (density 6-15% of total cells)
    horizontal run lengths: 1-7 pixels; multiple runs may share a row
    rows with obstacles: 3-26 rows occupied [observed]
  route_per_marker:
    algorithm: climb upward from marker column; at each ORANGE hit, exit right past the contiguous run on that row, then continue upward from exit column
    hits_per_route: 1-6 (turns/direction changes)
    termination: top-edge (marker at row 0) OR notch (cell flanked left+right by ORANGE with ORANGE roof above)
    notches_in_grid: 0-1 [observed]
  output_transform:
    vertical_approach cells (bg between segments) -> RED(2)
    hit ORANGE pixel -> TEAL(8); cell below hit -> YELLOW(4)
    horizontal under-run cells -> RED(2); right-exit cell -> GREEN(3)
    terminal cell -> MAGENTA(6) marker (row 0 or notch)
  constraints:
    routes must not overlap (no shared painted cells)
    right-exit column must be in-bounds and on bg
    all cells painted by route must be bg in original input
    notch structure: ORANGE at (r,c), bg at (r+1,c), ORANGE at (r+1,c-1) and (r+1,c+1)

