0004:   regions: 2-18 distinct 8-connected GREY regions in an ORANGE field
0005:   target_regions: 1-4 regions recolored GREY->TEAL(8); rest stay GREY
0006:   target_classification: |
0007:     Each 8-connected GREY region is decomposed into 4-connected lobes.
0008:     REQUIRED: a TEAL target contains a straight diagonal run of length >=3
0009:     pixels; diagonal-contact shapes whose longest straight diagonal run is
0010:     only 1-2 pixels remain GREY.
0011:     A region is recolored TEAL iff:
0012:       (a) single lobe forming a square-bbox diagonal staircase (bbox NxN, N>=4,
0013:           fill <=50%, occupies opposite corners NW+SE or NE+SW), OR
0014:       (b) multi-lobe: every lobe pair shares at most 1 diagonal contact direction,
0015:           lobes form a non-branching chain (max degree <=2), AND the region is
0016:           NOT: all singletons not on one diagonal line, all lobes on same border
0017:           side, or a 2-lobe (1-cell + >=5-cell) where not all lobes touch border.
0018:   target_region_stats:
0019:     size: 3-11 pixels
0020:     lobes: 1-4
0021:     diagonal_run: >=3 pixels
0022:   distractor_categories: |
0023:     - Single-lobe non-staircase blobs/bars/rectangles (most common)
0024:     - Isolated single pixels (size 1)
0025:     - Multi-lobe with branching (degree>2)
0026:     - Multi-lobe with multi-direction diagonal contact between a pair
0027:     - Multi-lobe chain but all lobes on same grid border
0028:     - All-singleton chain not along a single diagonal
0029:     - 2-lobe (singleton + large) where not both lobes touch grid border
0030: 
0031: generation_strategy:
0032:   approach: direct placement with classification guarantee
0033:   steps:
0034:     1. Choose grid size H x W in observed ranges.
0035:     2. Build 1-3 target regions (to be recolored):
0036:        - For staircase type, draw a square NxN (N=4-6) diagonal staircase
0037:          spanning opposite corners of its bbox; require a straight diagonal
0038:          run of length >=3.
0039:        - For chain type, grow 2-4 lobes connected by single diagonal contacts
0040:          in a non-branching chain; require a straight diagonal run of length
0041:          >=3 and ensure none of the rejection rules apply.
0042:     3. Build 3-15 distractor regions from varied categories:
0043:        - Compact 4-connected blobs (rectangles, L-shapes, bars) -- most common.
0044:        - Isolated single pixels scattered around.
0045:        - Optionally 1-2 near-miss distractors (chain with branching, or
0046:          multi-direction contact, or same-border-side chain) for difficulty.
0047:     4. Place all regions on the ORANGE grid ensuring 8-connected separation
0048:        between distinct regions (no two regions share an 8-neighbor).
0049:     5. Verify GREY density is 30-40%; adjust region count/sizes if needed.

